│                          │ each row and report per-row column orderings.                                             │
│                          │ - Honor col_merge by treating merged column groups as contiguous units (adjacency in each │
│                          │ row's ordering), without altering values.                                                 │
│                          │ - Build up to three cheap candidate orderings: (1) global frequency-ranked ordering using │
│                          │ sum(len(v)*count*(count-1)) per column, (2) a recursive conditional partition tree        │
│                          │ selecting the best length-weighted repetition column per group with depth/work bounds,    │
│                          │ (3) a deterministic alphabetical fallback.                                                │
│                          │ - Score each candidate by the true serial-Trie objective: serialize rows, sort, sum       │
│                          │ adjacent longest-common-prefix lengths (binary-search LCP so comparisons run in C). Pick  │
│                          │ the best.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Return the DataFrame with per-row permuted values (object dtype) plus a per-row         │
│                          │ column-ordering list consistent with the returned data, rows in original order.           │
