│ patch_name               │ rewrite_valid_rowwise_col_ordering                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The program failed validation because it broke the API contract: it returned an empty     │
│                          │ column_orderings list (no valid per-row orderings), mutated cell contents/columns (added  │
│                          │ an "original_index" column, merged/dropped columns, concatenated DataFrames with          │
│                          │ mismatched columns), relied on broken recursion (assigning rows via `result_df.loc` into  │
│                          │ an empty frame, `hasattr` attribute lookups on tuples, groupby on nonexistent columns),   │
│                          │ and used a squared-length objective unrelated to the actual serial character-Trie reuse.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fix: replace the editable algorithm with a correct, bounded implementation that (1)       │
│                          │ preserves every cell, row, and column exactly, (2) returns valid per-row column orderings │
│                          │ consistent with the returned DataFrame, (3) constructs a few cheap candidate global       │
│                          │ column orderings (length-weighted repetition count·(count−1)·len ranking, count·(count−1) │
│                          │ ranking, and original order), scores each with the true serial-Trie objective (sum of     │
│                          │ adjacent LCPs over sorted serialized rows, computed with C-speed slice-equality binary    │
│                          │ search), and returns the best. col_merge groups are kept contiguous in the ordering,      │
│                          │ honoring merge adjacency without altering data. NaN/mixed types are handled by            │
│                          │ normalizing only the scoring serialization string ("" for missing), never modifying       │
│                          │ stored values.                                                                            │
