│ patch_name               │ rewrite_trie_prefix_candidates                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The previous program failed validation because its recursive value-grouping pipeline      │
│                          │ produced inconsistent shapes/orderings: it split into `grouped_rows`/`remaining_rows` and │
│                          │ recombined DataFrames via `pd.concat`/`update` with positional `loc` inserts,             │
│                          │ dropped/merged columns, appended an `original_index` helper column, sorted rows, and      │
│                          │ finally returned an empty `column_orderings` list — so per-row column orderings were not  │
│                          │ consistent with the returned data (and cell/shape preservation assertions could fail on   │
│                          │ mixed-type data). The whole approach also optimized squared field lengths on a single     │
│                          │ "max group value" rather than actual character-prefix reuse.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fix: replace the editable block with a correct, bounded construction-selection algorithm. │
│                          │ - Serialize each cell exactly as the evaluator does (missing → ""), factorize columns     │
│                          │ once into integer codes, and precompute value lengths.                                    │
│                          │ - Build up to three cheap per-row column-ordering candidates: (1) a global                │
│                          │ frequency-ranked order scoring each column as sum(len(v)*count*(count-1)), (2) the        │
│                          │ original column order, and (3) a recursive conditional partition tree that picks, inside  │
│                          │ each row group, the remaining column with the largest length-weighted pair repetition,    │
│                          │ partitions rows by that column's codes, and orders suffixes per group (bounded depth 8,   │
│                          │ bounded candidate columns, deterministic global-order tail).                              │
│                          │ - Score candidates with the exact serial Trie objective (sum of adjacent LCPs of the      │
│                          │ sorted serialized rows, using C-speed slice-equality binary search), pick the best; skip  │
│                          │ scoring with a safe heuristic fallback when the data is too large.                        │
│                          │ - One-way dependencies are enforced by moving each dependent column right after its       │
│                          │ source in every row order; col_merge groups are merged into a single concatenated column  │
│                          │ (serialization is unchanged since fields have no separators), preserving API semantics.   │
│                          │ - The output DataFrame keeps the original row order/index, object dtype, and returns      │
│                          │ per-row column name orderings matching the positional data exactly, with no fabricated,   │
│                          │ dropped, or altered cells.                                                                │
