│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ clean_prefix_cache_reorder                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The original code was deeply broken: it mutated/merged columns (col_merge paths changed   │
│                          │ shapes), returned an empty column_orderings list (invalid per-row orderings), fabricated  │
│                          │ an "original_index" column, reordered via fragile itertuples/attribute lookups, used      │
│                          │ threading with non-deterministic row assignment (futures assigned by as_completed index), │
│                          │ and its final sort reordered rows without consistent per-row column orders. The fix       │
│                          │ replaces the entire editable block with a simple, correct, deterministic implementation:  │
│                          │ serialize each cell to its scoring string once, build up to three cheap candidate per-row │
│                          │ column orderings (frequency-ranked global order, length-weighted count*(count-1) order,   │
│                          │ original order), score each candidate exactly via the sorted-string adjacent-LCP sum      │
